{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>When a fire goes out.</b> This too is connected, for it speaks of damage to a field." "And the meaning of המבעיר is not like יבעיר איש (Exodus 22:4), even though they are of one binyan, for the word אש governs it. And this is an elegant device in the holy tongue: to use an identical word, and it is for two reasons, as in על לחי החמור חמור חמורתים (Judges 15:16); רוכבים על שלשים עַיָרִים, and שלשים עירים להם (Judges 10:4) — and this second one [means] cities, and the proof: להם יקראו חות יאיר (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:22.685641723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}